{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XveMjzgi3xzMoK3VkeGHir","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me create a final comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've analyzed how error-case differential tests handle stderr normalization in this go-unix-utils repo. Here are the key patterns across 4+ test utilities:\n\n### **Core Pattern: DiffTest Structure**\n\nFrom `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5461/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`:\n- **DiffTest struct fields:**\n  - `ExitCode`: Set to non-zero (typically 1) for error cases\n  - `Normalize`: Slice of `NormalizeFunc` applied to both stdout and stderr before comparison\n  - `NormalizeFunc` is a type alias: `type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte`\n\n---\n\n### **Pattern 1: Regex-based Binary Name Normalization (sort)**\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5461/cmd/sort/sort_test.go` (lines 16-23)\n\n```go\nvar progRe = regexp.MustCompile(`(?m)^(\\S*/)?g?sort:`)\nvar tryRe = regexp.MustCompile(`'(\\S*/)?g?sort --help'`)\n\nfunc normStderr(b []byte) []byte {\n\tb = progRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"PROG:\"))\n\tb = tryRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"'PROG --help'\"))\n\treturn b\n}\n```\n\n**Used for error cases:**\n- `check_unsorted` (line 181-186): Detects when input is not sorted\n- `check_numeric_unsorted` (line 206-211): Numeric sort validation\n- `check_unique_fail` (line 219-224): Duplicate detection\n- `check_reverse_unsorted` (line 232-237): Reverse sort validation\n- `invalid_long_flag` (line 263-267): Invalid option handling\n\n---\n\n### **Pattern 2: Composable Normalizer Functions (cut)**\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5461/cmd/cut/cut_test.go` (lines 27-37)\n\n```go\nbinaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?cut`)\nnormalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n\treturn binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"cut\"))\n})\nnormalizeErrCase := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n\treturn bytes.ToLower(b)\n})\nnormalizeOpenPrefix := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n\treturn bytes.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\": open \"), []byte(\": \"))\n})\nerrNorm := []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName, normalizeErrCase, normalizeOpenPrefix}\n```\n\n**Applied to file errors:**\n- `nonexistent_file` (line 61-66): ExitCode: 1, uses `errNorm`\n- `nonexistent_then_valid` (line 68-73): ExitCode: 1, uses `errNorm`\n- `valid_then_nonexistent` (line 75-80): ExitCode: 1, uses `errNorm`\n\n---\n\n### **Pattern 3: Line-by-line Regex Normalization (comm)**\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5461/cmd/comm/comm_test.go` (lines 21-36)\n\n```go\nvar stderrNorm = regexp.MustCompile(`^g?comm:`)\n\nfunc normStderr(b []byte) []byte {\n\tvar out []byte\n\tfor line := range bytes.SplitSeq(b, []byte(\"\\n\")) {\n\t\tif len(out) > 0 {\n\t\t\tout = append(out, '\\n')\n\t\t}\n\t\tout = append(out, stderrNorm.ReplaceAll(line, []byte(\"PROG:\"))...)\n\t}\n\treturn out\n}\n\nfunc normStderrLower(b []byte) []byte {\n\treturn bytes.ToLower(normStderr(b))\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Pattern 4: Total Discard of Stderr (head)**\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5461/cmd/head/head_test.go` (line 23)\n\n```go\ndiscardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n```\n\n**Used for file not found errors:**\n- `nonexistent-only` (ExitCode: 1)\n- `bytes-invalid` (ExitCode: 1)\n- Multiple file permutations with missing files\n\n---\n\n### **Pattern 5: Selective Prefix Filtering (expr)**\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5461/cmd/expr/expr_test.go`\n\n```go\nnormBinName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n\treturn bytes.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"gexpr:\"), []byte(\"expr:\"))\n})\nnormStripTry := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n\tvar out []byte\n\tfor line := range bytes.SplitSeq(b, []byte(\"\\n\")) {\n\t\tif bytes.HasPrefix(line, []byte(\"Try \")) {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\t// ... append to out\n\t}\n\treturn out\n})\n```\n\n**Error test names:**\n- `div_by_zero`, `mod_by_zero`: Math errors\n- `err_missing_operand`, `err_unclosed_paren`, `err_unexpected_arg`: Syntax errors\n- `err_missing_all`: No arguments provided\n\n---\n\n### **Key Takeaways for join:**\n\n1. **Use `ExitCode` field** for non-zero cases (typically 1 for file/option errors)\n2. **Create a regex normalizer** matching the pattern `(?m)^(\\S*/)?gjoin:` to convert both \"join:\" and \"gjoin:\" to a canonical form\n3. **Apply normalization only to error cases** via the `Normalize` field\n4. **Compose multiple normalizers** if needed (binary name + case normalization + output prefix fixes)\n5. **Test errors early**: missing files, invalid options, unsorted inputs (if applicable)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"deaea588-c295-41cb-8cb1-943a952dfad4","uuid":"f0f0e245-e24b-421a-bda6-4075a1f8ed70","timestamp":"2026-05-22T14:56:54.744Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5461, I need to understand how other cmd/ utilities handle error-case differential tests where stderr messages differ by program name (e.g., \"join:\" vs \"gjoin:\"). \n\nLook at a few cmd/*/test files to find DiffTest entries that test error conditions (missing file, invalid option, etc.) and see how they handle stderr normalization. Search for patterns like:\n- Normalize fields in DiffTest structs\n- NormalizeFunc usage  \n- Tests with non-zero ExitCode\n- Error case test names\n\nCheck 3-4 different cmd/ directories. Quick search.","agentId":"a6b9684acc68946e7","agentType":"Explore","content":[{